### Steward walkthrough (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP client)
### Phase 2: every API call needs credentials. Start the server; on first boot it prints a generated
### admin password (or set STEWARD_ADMIN_PASSWORD before the first boot).
@base = http://127.0.0.1:3000
@adminPassword = change-me

### Health (public)
GET {{base}}/health

### 0. Log in as admin -> copy result.token into @token
# @name login
POST {{base}}/api/steward/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "user_name": "admin", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.result.token}}

### Who am I?
GET {{base}}/api/steward/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 1. Create the root "task" table
POST {{base}}/api/steward/meta/tables
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "task",
  "fields": [
    { "element": "number", "type": "string" },
    { "element": "short_description", "type": "string", "maxLength": 160, "mandatory": true },
    { "element": "priority", "type": "integer", "defaultValue": 4 },
    { "element": "state", "type": "choice", "defaultValue": "new",
      "choices": [ { "value": "new", "label": "New" }, { "value": "closed", "label": "Closed" } ] },
    { "element": "assigned_to", "type": "reference", "reference": "sys_user" },
    { "element": "caller", "type": "reference", "reference": "sys_user" },
    { "element": "work_notes", "type": "text" }
  ]
}

### 2. Extend it: incident (auto-numbered INC...)
POST {{base}}/api/steward/meta/tables
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "incident", "extends": "task", "numberPrefix": "INC" }

### 3. Inspect the resolved schema (inherited fields, storage columns)
GET {{base}}/api/steward/meta/tables/incident
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Create a role "itil" -> note its sys_id
POST {{base}}/api/now/table/sys_user_role
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "itil" }

### 5. Create two users (passwords are hashed and never returned)
POST {{base}}/api/now/table/sys_user
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "user_name": "alice", "first_name": "Alice", "user_password": "alice-pw" }

###
POST {{base}}/api/now/table/sys_user
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "user_name": "carol", "first_name": "Carol", "user_password": "carol-pw" }

### 6. Give alice the itil role
POST {{base}}/api/now/table/sys_user_has_role
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "user": "<alice sys_id>", "role": "<itil sys_id>" }

### 7. ACLs (admin has security_admin): itil reads all tasks; everyone reads tasks where they are the caller;
###    only itil reads work_notes. Then link roles via sys_security_acl_role.
POST {{base}}/api/now/table/sys_security_acl
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "task", "operation": "read", "description": "itil reads all tasks" }

###
POST {{base}}/api/now/table/sys_security_acl_role
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sys_security_acl": "<acl sys_id from above>", "sys_user_role": "<itil sys_id>" }

###
POST {{base}}/api/now/table/sys_security_acl
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "task", "operation": "read", "condition": "caller=javascript:gs.getUserID()", "description": "callers read their own" }

###
POST {{base}}/api/now/table/sys_security_acl
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "task.work_notes", "operation": "read", "description": "itil only" }

###
POST {{base}}/api/now/table/sys_security_acl_role
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sys_security_acl": "<work_notes acl sys_id>", "sys_user_role": "<itil sys_id>" }

### 8. Create incidents (one with carol as caller)
POST {{base}}/api/now/table/incident
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "short_description": "Carol's printer", "caller": "<carol sys_id>", "work_notes": "VIP" }

###
POST {{base}}/api/now/table/incident
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "short_description": "Someone else's VPN", "work_notes": "internal" }

### 9. Same query, different users (Basic auth: alice:alice-pw / carol:carol-pw)
GET {{base}}/api/now/table/incident?sysparm_fields=number,short_description,work_notes
Authorization: Basic alice:alice-pw

###
GET {{base}}/api/now/table/incident?sysparm_fields=number,short_description,work_notes
Authorization: Basic carol:carol-pw

### 10. Impersonate carol with the admin token, look, then stop
POST {{base}}/api/steward/auth/impersonate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "user_name": "carol" }

###
GET {{base}}/api/now/table/incident?sysparm_fields=number,short_description
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
DELETE {{base}}/api/steward/auth/impersonate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Dot-walk + display values, optimistic update, audit (as admin)
GET {{base}}/api/now/table/incident?sysparm_query=priority<=4^ORDERBYDESCsys_created_on&sysparm_fields=number,caller,caller.user_name,state&sysparm_display_value=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
PATCH {{base}}/api/now/table/incident/<sys_id>
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "0"

{ "priority": 1 }

###
GET {{base}}/api/now/table/sys_audit?sysparm_query=documentkey=<sys_id>^ORDERBYrecord_checkpoint&sysparm_fields=fieldname,oldvalue,newvalue,user,record_checkpoint
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Log out
POST {{base}}/api/steward/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
